OPTIONAL MCP SERVER (mcp-server/, docker compose profile "mcp")
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MCP server has its own dependency set, inventoried in:

    mcp-server/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md

Dependencies there with obligations that survive redistribution:

  * paramiko            - LGPL-2.1
  * certifi             - MPL-2.0
  * orjson              - MPL-2.0 AND (Apache-2.0 OR MIT)

Its image adds Debian packages, among them git and iproute2 (GPL-2.0), under
the same source offer as above. The profile also runs two upstream images that
CoreSpan does not build or modify: agentgateway (Apache-2.0) and
tecnativa/docker-socket-proxy (Apache-2.0, on an HAProxy base, GPL-2.0). Their
inventories are in sbom/ (make sbom-mcp).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPTIONAL AGENT RUNNER (agent-runner/, docker compose profile "mcp")
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The agent runner has its own dependency set, inventoried in:

    agent-runner/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md

Dependencies there with obligations that survive redistribution:

  * psycopg, psycopg-binary, psycopg-pool - LGPL-3.0
  * certifi             - MPL-2.0
  * orjson              - MPL-2.0 AND (Apache-2.0 OR MIT)

Its image is python:3.11-slim with no added Debian packages; its inventory is in
sbom/ (make sbom-mcp). The LLM it calls, and that model's weights, are supplied
by the site under their own licences (see the next section).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPTIONAL SANDBOX MCP SERVER (sandbox-mcp/, docker compose profile "mcp")
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The sandbox MCP server has its own dependency set, inventoried in:

    sandbox-mcp/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md

Dependencies there with obligations that survive redistribution:

  * certifi             - MPL-2.0

It runs programs in containers under gVisor (runsc, Apache-2.0), which the site
installs on its Docker host; CoreSpan does not ship gVisor. The sandbox image
(python:3.11-slim by default) is pulled from Docker Hub under its own licences.

